    pr_ref:  # 3a07
    description: "In the message-queue linker, when a publish topic is a variable, `topic_type=variable` is emitted and the stored topic value is the variable IDENTIFIER (`topic`/`TOPIC`/`EVENTS_TOPIC`) rather than its resolved string value; the same publisher emits both `literal` and `variable` for one logical topic depending on subscriber fan-out. A consumer joining publishers↔subscribers by topic value cannot match a variable-topic publish to its literal-topic subscriber. Fix: resolve the topic variable to its assigned value in message_queue.py topic extraction (or label it unresolved rather than storing the identifier as if it were the value). Surfaced via dogfooding; blinded severity 3/5."  # 3a07
    fields: {}  # 3a07
